<!-- ========== THESIS ========== -->
<section id="thesis">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">01 · Thesis</div>
    <h2 class="stitle">Your health lives in a dozen apps. No one reads it as a whole.</h2>

    <div class="thesis-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="clamp-mob">DNA in one report, wearables in another, labs in a PDF, microbiome on a third site. Each sees one fragment; the patterns live <em>between</em> them. VitaCrypt fuses all of it into one profile and reads it together, against your genotype and your environment, then returns guidance that cites its source.</p>
        <p class="clamp-mob"><strong>Privacy is what makes centralizing it acceptable.</strong> The most valuable signals are the ones you should trust the fewest companies with, so the platform is built private by design: your phone encrypts under a key you hold (iOS&nbsp;Keychain / Android&nbsp;Keystore) and analysis is built to run on ciphertext. Blind compute is proven today on one encrypted genetic vector; the rest of the pipeline is what this build scales.<sup><a href="litepaper.html#threat">1</a></sup></p>
      </div>
      <div class="right" data-mcollapse="The four failures we replace">
        <h4>The four failures we replace</h4>
        <div class="item">
          <strong>Fragmentation</strong>
          Wearables, DNA kits, labs, and doctors all hold pieces. The patterns live <em>between</em> them.
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <strong>Exposed plaintext</strong>
          "At-rest encryption" is marketing. Analysis still decrypts on someone else's server.
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <strong>Generic advice</strong>
          Optimized for the median person. Ignores genotype, microbiome, and local context.
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <strong>Environmental blindness</strong>
          No tool fuses outdoor air, exposures, and biology against <em>your</em> vulnerabilities.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== DATA FABRIC ========== -->
<section id="fabric">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">02 · The data fabric</div>
    <h2 class="stitle">Six streams of biology. One queryable profile.</h2>
    <p class="lede clamp-mob">Encryption is one pillar; the other is the scope of what we unify. Wearable APIs (unified via <strong>Terra API</strong>), open environmental data, lab results, microbiome assays, genetic reports, and NIH-validated <strong>PROMIS</strong> short-forms, all pulled together on the device, in your possession, before anything is encrypted or transmitted.</p>

    <div class="fabric-wrap">
      <span class="fabric-swipe-hint">Swipe all six sources →</span>
      <div class="fabric-grid">
        <div class="fabric-card">
          <div class="hd">
            <span class="ix">SOURCE 01</span>
            <span class="ic">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 3c0 4 8 4 8 8M11 3c0 4-8 4-8 8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" stroke-linecap="round"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <h4>Genetics</h4>
          <p class="why">DNA reports surface variants that change what every other recommendation should mean for this person: folate cycle, lipid handling, methylation, caffeine clearance, exercise response.</p>
          <div class="sources">
            <span class="src">23andMe</span>
            <span class="src">AncestryDNA</span>
            <span class="src">Nebula WGS</span>
            <span class="src">Self-decoded raw</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fabric-card">
          <div class="hd">
            <span class="ix">SOURCE 02</span>
            <span class="ic">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><rect x="4" y="2" width="6" height="10" rx="1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1"/><circle cx="7" cy="10" r="0.7" fill="currentColor"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <h4>Wearables</h4>
          <p class="why">Continuous physiology: HRV, resting heart, sleep stages, recovery, respiration, body temperature, daily activity load. The minute-by-minute reaction to everything else we measure.</p>
          <div class="sources">
            <span class="src live">Apple Watch</span>
            <span class="src live">Oura</span>
            <span class="src live">Whoop</span>
            <span class="src">Fitbit</span>
            <span class="src">Garmin</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fabric-card">
          <div class="hd">
            <span class="ix">SOURCE 03</span>
            <span class="ic">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M5 2v4l-2.5 5.2a1 1 0 0 0 .9 1.4h7.2a1 1 0 0 0 .9-1.4L9 6V2M4 2h6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <h4>Labs &amp; blood</h4>
          <p class="why">CRP, ApoB, fasting glucose, HbA1c, vitamin D, B12, iron, lipid panels. The objective check against the wearable signal, what your physiology is actually doing under the skin.</p>
          <div class="sources">
            <span class="src">Manual upload</span>
            <span class="src">Quest portal</span>
            <span class="src">LabCorp portal</span>
            <span class="src">Function Health</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fabric-card">
          <div class="hd">
            <span class="ix">SOURCE 04</span>
            <span class="ic">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><circle cx="4.5" cy="4.5" r="1.6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1"/><circle cx="9.5" cy="6.5" r="2" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1"/><circle cx="5.5" cy="10" r="1.4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <h4>Microbiome</h4>
          <p class="why">Gut composition shapes inflammation, mood, nutrient absorption, and how a person responds to any dietary protocol. The map between food, stress, and outcome only makes sense with it.</p>
          <div class="sources">
            <span class="src">Viome</span>
            <span class="src">Tiny Health</span>
            <span class="src">Sun Genomics</span>
            <span class="src">Bristol surveys</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fabric-card">
          <div class="hd">
            <span class="ix">SOURCE 05</span>
            <span class="ic">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><circle cx="7" cy="7" r="5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1"/><path d="M2 7h10M7 2c1.5 2 1.5 8 0 10M7 2c-1.5 2-1.5 8 0 10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="0.9"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <h4>Environment</h4>
          <p class="why">PM2.5, ozone, pollen, UV, indoor humidity, water quality, ambient noise. The boundary condition every cell in the body is reacting to in real time, and the one most people never see.</p>
          <div class="sources">
            <span class="src live">PurpleAir</span>
            <span class="src live">IQAir</span>
            <span class="src live">OpenWeather</span>
            <span class="src">NASA AQ</span>
            <span class="src">USGS water</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="fabric-card is-profile">
          <div class="hd">
            <span class="ix">SOURCE 06</span>
            <span class="ic">
              <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none"><path d="M3 11v-2a4 4 0 1 1 8 0v2M7 6.5a2 2 0 1 0 0-4 2 2 0 0 0 0 4Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1"/></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <h4>Lifestyle &amp; PROMIS</h4>
          <p class="why">Stress, sleep quality, mood, diet logs, supplement stack, work load, captured via NIH-validated <strong>PROMIS</strong> short-forms. The user's <strong>own annotation</strong> of why this week looks the way it does, context the data alone won't surface.</p>
          <div class="sources">
            <span class="src">Daily check-in</span>
            <span class="src">Symptom diary</span>
            <span class="src">Supplement log</span>
            <span class="src">PROMIS short-form</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="fabric-foot">
        <div class="l">All six streams resolve into <strong>one unified profile</strong> on your device · then encrypted under your key before any byte leaves.</div>
        <div class="legend">
          <span><span class="dot"></span>Direct API · at MVP launch</span>
          <span><span class="dot q"></span>Upload / partner</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== LIVE RESEARCH (Pillar 3) ========== -->
<section id="research">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">03 · Live science</div>
    <h2 class="stitle">Every recommendation cites its source.</h2>
    <p class="lede clamp-mob">Most health apps tell you what was true in 2018. We tell you what was published this week. Recommendations re-evaluate every time a new paper, GWAS hit, or regulatory update lands in one of the corpora below.</p>

    <div class="research-corpora" data-mcollapse="The 8 sources we query live">
      <div class="corpus">
        <div class="nm"><span class="dot"></span>PubMed</div>
        <p class="why">~40M indexed records · NLM open data · queried live</p>
      </div>
      <div class="corpus">
        <div class="nm"><span class="dot"></span>OpenAlex</div>
        <p class="why">~250M scholarly works · open-access first ranking · full text where licensed</p>
      </div>
      <div class="corpus">
        <div class="nm"><span class="dot"></span>GWAS Catalog</div>
        <p class="why">Variant-trait associations · curated genome-wide hits · EBI/NHGRI</p>
      </div>
      <div class="corpus">
        <div class="nm"><span class="dot"></span>ClinVar</div>
        <p class="why">Variant-clinical-significance mapping · NCBI · daily updates</p>
      </div>
      <div class="corpus">
        <div class="nm"><span class="dot"></span>USPSTF</div>
        <p class="why">US Preventive Services Task Force · grade A/B recommendations</p>
      </div>
      <div class="corpus">
        <div class="nm"><span class="dot"></span>WHO</div>
        <p class="why">Global clinical guidance · WHO Guidelines · cohort & trial data</p>
      </div>
      <div class="corpus">
        <div class="nm"><span class="dot"></span>NICE</div>
        <p class="why">UK National Institute for Health and Care Excellence · clinical pathways</p>
      </div>
      <div class="corpus">
        <div class="nm"><span class="dot"></span>Cochrane</div>
        <p class="why">~4,500 systematic reviews · evidence weighting · meta-analysis</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="research-arch">
      <div class="k">Architecture</div>
      <div>
        <p>An agent watches the public science for you, across all eight corpora above. <strong>The model only reads public papers.</strong> The architecture is built so the match between a paper's findings and your profile happens <strong>under FHE, cryptographically, rather than by sending your data anywhere</strong>; moving the full matching pipeline behind that guarantee is the current build.</p>
        <div class="out">Full source menu, model layer, and matching protocol in the <a href="litepaper.html#engine">litepaper →</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== PIPELINE — combined arch + live demo ========== -->
<section id="pipeline">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">04 · The architecture</div>
    <h2 class="stitle">How VitaCrypt is built to work.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Click any stage. The architecture, the encryption state, and the phone respond together. Auto-plays on first scroll. This walkthrough shows the target design; blind compute is proven today on one encrypted genetic vector (~0.5s, the server never holds the key) and the round scales it across the full pipeline.</p>

    <div class="pipe-wrap">
      <div class="pipe-head">
        <div class="ttl"><span id="pipeHeadLabel">STAGE 01 / COLLECT</span></div>
        <div class="pipe-tabs">
          <button class="active" data-step="0">01 COLLECT</button>
          <button data-step="1">02 ENCRYPT</button>
          <button data-step="2">03 COMPUTE</button>
          <button data-step="3">04 ACT</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pipe-body">
        <!-- LEFT: explanation in plain language -->
        <div class="pipe-explain">
          <div class="stage-tag"><span class="box" id="stTagBox">01</span> <span id="stTagText">COLLECT</span></div>
          <h3 id="stTitle">A unified profile, drawn from every source.</h3>
          <div class="summary" id="stSummary">
            Wearables (via Terra API), DNA, microbiome, labs, environment, and PROMIS surveys ingest on-device into a single living profile. <strong>Nothing has left the device yet.</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="what">
            <div class="lbl">What this looks like in practice</div>
            <ul id="stWhatList">
              <li>Upload 23andMe / AncestryDNA reports</li>
              <li>Connect Apple Watch or Oura ring</li>
              <li>Pull air-quality + UV from your location</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- MIDDLE: visual architecture -->
        <div class="pipe-arch">
          <div class="arch-stage">
            <div class="arch-key left" id="archKeyLeft">🔑 KEY · ON DEVICE</div>
            <div class="arch-key middle" id="archKeyMiddle">CIPHERTEXT ONLY</div>
            <div class="arch-key right" id="archKeyRight">🔑 KEY · ON DEVICE</div>

            <div class="arch-node left" id="archLeft">
              <div class="frame active">
                <div class="ringer"></div>
                <div class="content">
                  <div class="bar tall"></div>
                  <div class="bar short"></div>
                  <div class="bar teal"></div>
                  <div class="bar short"></div>
                  <div class="bar"></div>
                  <div class="bar short"></div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="label">Your device<span class="sub">Raw biology</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="arch-node server center" id="archCenter">
              <div class="frame">
                <div class="content">
                  <div class="lat">VITACRYPT COMPUTE</div>
                  <div class="ct"></div>
                  <div class="lat">// no decryption</div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="label">FHE compute<span class="sub">On ciphertext</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="arch-node right" id="archRight">
              <div class="frame">
                <div class="ringer"></div>
                <div class="content">
                  <div class="bar short"></div>
                  <div class="bar tall"></div>
                  <div class="bar teal"></div>
                  <div class="bar"></div>
                  <div class="bar short teal"></div>
                  <div class="bar"></div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="label">Your device<span class="sub">Insight, decrypted</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="arch-flow">
              <div class="arch-spacer"></div>
              <div class="arch-arrow" id="archArrow1">
                <span class="lbl">encrypt →</span>
                <svg viewBox="0 0 100 28" preserveAspectRatio="none">
                  <line class="line" x1="2" y1="14" x2="92" y2="14"/>
                  <polygon class="arrowhead" points="92,9 100,14 92,19"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="arch-spacer wide"></div>
              <div class="arch-arrow" id="archArrow2">
                <span class="lbl">return ciphertext →</span>
                <svg viewBox="0 0 100 28" preserveAspectRatio="none">
                  <line class="line" x1="2" y1="14" x2="92" y2="14"/>
                  <polygon class="arrowhead" points="92,9 100,14 92,19"/>
                </svg>
              </div>
              <div class="arch-spacer"></div>
            </div>

            <div class="arch-foot">KEYS NEVER LEAVE THE TWO DEVICES</div>
