</section>

<!-- ========== DIFFERENTIATION ========== -->
<section id="diff">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">05 · Versus the field</div>
    <h2 class="stitle">Unified health profiles always meant centralized databases. Until now.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Keep your Oura. Keep your Apple Watch. Keep your Whoop. We connect to all of them, and add what they can't see. Three axes where the consumer health stack breaks down, and what we do instead.</p>

    <div class="diff-banner">
      <div class="hd">What only VitaCrypt adds, beyond your wearable</div>
      <div class="diff-banner-grid">
        <div class="item">
          <h4><span class="ix">01</span>DNA &amp; genetics</h4>
          <p>Upload 23andMe / AncestryDNA / Nebula WGS, parsed into your unified profile.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <h4><span class="ix">02</span>Microbiome</h4>
          <p>Upload Tiny Health, Viome, or uBiome, gut signal in context with everything else.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <h4><span class="ix">03</span>Labs &amp; hormones</h4>
          <p>Bring your own from Quest, Labcorp, Function, Superpower. We don't resell tests.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="item">
          <h4><span class="ix">04</span>Live environment</h4>
          <p>PM2.5, pollen, UV from AirNow / OpenWeather / Pollen API at your exact location.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="footnote">
        <span class="k">Privacy moat</span>And the only one in this category built so data never leaves your device in the clear. <em>npj Digital Medicine</em> (2025) flagged Oura, Whoop, and Fitbit for permissive data-sharing terms.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="diff-grid" data-mcollapse="See the three-way comparison">
      <div class="diff-card">
        <div class="ix">01 · DATA SCOPE</div>
        <h3>One slice doesn't see the pattern.</h3>
        <p>Wearables know sleep. DNA kits know genes. Labs know markers. No single tool fuses six layers against your local environment in real time.</p>
        <div class="vs">
          <div class="row them"><span class="k">Others</span><span>One silo (wearable / DNA / labs).</span></div>
          <div class="row us"><span class="k">VitaCrypt</span><span>Six layers, unified, contextualized.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="diff-card">
        <div class="ix">02 · OWNERSHIP</div>
        <h3>You hold the only key.</h3>
        <p>In the consumer health stack, you are the data and the data is the asset. We're built to invert that: your key, on your hardware, is the only way the insights become readable.</p>
        <div class="vs">
          <div class="row them"><span class="k">Others</span><span>Platform owns and monetizes data.</span></div>
          <div class="row us"><span class="k">VitaCrypt</span><span>Your key, by design; built so we can't read it.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="diff-card">
        <div class="ix">03 · ENCRYPTION</div>
        <h3>Decrypt to compute, or don't compute.</h3>
        <p>Every player in the category encrypts at rest, then decrypts the moment they want to look at it. A breach is permanent: you can rotate a password, not a genome.</p>
        <div class="vs">
          <div class="row them"><span class="k">Others</span><span>At-rest only. Plaintext during compute.</span></div>
          <div class="row us"><span class="k">VitaCrypt</span><span>FHE by design; blind compute proven on one slice today.</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ========== CASE ========== -->
<section id="case">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">06 · Case study</div>
    <h2 class="stitle">25, Los Angeles, breathing on the 97th percentile.</h2>
    <p class="lede">A composite case from the litepaper. Values illustrative, methodology real.</p>

    <div class="case-wrap">
      <div class="case-grid">
        <div class="case-profile">
          <div class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" fill="none">
              <circle cx="32" cy="26" r="8.5" fill="rgba(244,245,242,0.92)"/>
              <path d="M14 64 c0 -11 8 -19 18 -19 s18 8 18 19" fill="rgba(244,245,242,0.92)"/>
              <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="30" stroke="color-mix(in srgb, var(--teal) 40%, transparent)" stroke-width="0.8" stroke-dasharray="2 3" fill="none"/>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <h4>David</h4>
          <div class="role">Engineer, Echo Park</div>
          <div class="fields">
            <div><span class="k">Age</span><span class="v">25</span></div>
            <div><span class="k">PM2.5 zone</span><span class="v">p97</span></div>
            <div><span class="k">MTHFR</span><span class="v">C677T (TT)</span></div>
            <div><span class="k">APOE</span><span class="v">3/4</span></div>
            <div><span class="k">Wearable</span><span class="v">Apple Watch</span></div>
            <div><span class="k">Sources</span><span class="v">5</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="case-narrative">
          <h3>Healthy on paper, until you connect the signals.</h3>
          <p class="clamp-mob">David sleeps seven hours, exercises four times a week, eats well. He also lives where ambient PM2.5 routinely exceeds the WHO guideline by 5×, carries an <strong>MTHFR C677T (TT)</strong> variant that blunts folate-to-5MTHF conversion (his homocysteine runs high on a "normal" diet), and an <strong>APOE ε3/ε4</strong> that makes him cardiovascularly sensitive to the air his commute pipes into his lungs. No single app sees both. VitaCrypt does.</p>

          <div class="insight-box">
            <div class="lbl">VitaCrypt insight</div>
            <div class="body">"Your MTHFR TT plus PM2.5 p97 plus a 22% HRV decline indicates sustained low-grade inflammatory pressure on a vascular system your APOE 3/4 already taxes. Activate home HEPA on forecast windows; supplement <em>methylated</em> folate (5-MTHF) + DHA; shift cardio to the 6–9am low-AQI window."</div>
          </div>

          <div data-mcollapse="Show the protocol &amp; privacy guarantee">
            <h3>The protocol</h3>
            <div class="protocol">
              <div class="row"><span class="tag">DIET</span><span class="txt">Methylated folate (5-MTHF), DHA-rich foods, prebiotic fiber for stress-driven dysbiosis.</span></div>
              <div class="row"><span class="tag">ENV</span><span class="txt">HEPA auto-triggers when forecast AQI &gt; 100. Outdoor cardio reschedules to 6–9am.</span></div>
              <div class="row"><span class="tag">RECOVERY</span><span class="txt">Replace one HIIT/week with zone-2 cardio until HRV recovers ≥10%.</span></div>
              <div class="row"><span class="tag">TRACKING</span><span class="txt">Re-evaluate inflammatory markers in 8 weeks, encrypted intake.</span></div>
            </div>

            <h3>What never happened</h3>
            <p>At no point did David's genotype, his HRV time series, or his location-bound PM2.5 exposure exist on a VitaCrypt server in a form anyone could read. <strong>The economics of a breach collapse when ciphertext is all that lives on the other side.</strong></p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="case-device">
          <div class="col-lbl">// what david receives</div>
          <div class="mini-phone">
            <div class="mini-screen">
              <div class="alert">
                <div class="h">⚡ Tomorrow · 14:00</div>
                <div class="b">PM2.5 forecast 78 μg/m³. HEPA armed. Outdoor cardio rescheduled to 7am.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="alert" style="background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(245,199,126,0.1), rgba(245,199,126,0.02)); border-color: rgba(245,199,126,0.3);">
                <div class="h" style="color: var(--amber);">🧬 Tonight</div>
                <div class="b">Add 5-MTHF 800µg with dinner. Skip standard folic acid.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="row-3">
                <div class="chip">
                  <div class="l">HRV trend</div>
                  <div class="v">↓ 22%</div>
                  <div class="delta">6-week</div>
                </div>
                <div class="chip">
                  <div class="l">CRP</div>
                  <div class="v">3.2<span class="u">mg/L</span></div>
                  <div class="delta" style="color: var(--amber);">Borderline</div>
                </div>
                <div class="chip">
                  <div class="l">Sleep</div>
                  <div class="v">7h12</div>
                  <div class="delta">On target</div>
                </div>
                <div class="chip">
                  <div class="l">Cites</div>
                  <div class="v">+4</div>
                  <div class="delta">PubMed</div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

