<!-- ========== WHY NOW ========== -->
<section id="why">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">09 · Why now</div>
    <h2 class="stitle">The signals, the demand and the technology all arrived at once.</h2>
    <p class="lede">Enough people now carry genetic, wearable and lab data to make a unified profile meaningful; the category has serious capital; and the privacy technology that lets a person trust one app with all of it finally shipped. As external corroboration, Zama's encrypted-DNA benchmark hit <strong>96% ancestry-classification accuracy</strong> (<a href="https://github.com/zama-ai/bounty-program/issues/95">bounty #95</a>, 2024), evidence the field's primitive works. The gap is that no one has put these together.</p>

    <div class="kpi-grid">
      <div class="kpi">
        <div class="label">UNIFICATION</div>
        <div class="val">6<span class="unit">&nbsp;in 1</span></div>
        <div class="desc">Genetics, wearables, labs, microbiome, environment and lifestyle, fused into a single profile. The unification no current product offers</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi">
        <div class="label">CATEGORY CAPITAL</div>
        <div class="val">$30<span class="unit">M</span></div>
        <div class="desc">Superpower's Series&nbsp;A (Apr 2025, &gt;$300M post). Function Health and others are racing the consumer-health-data land grab, none unifying it privately</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi">
        <div class="label">23ANDME FALLOUT</div>
        <div class="val">6.9<span class="unit">M</span></div>
        <div class="desc">Users breached · $30M settlement, £2.31M ICO fine, Chapter 11, sold for $305M (2023–25)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="kpi">
        <div class="label">STAGING PROOF</div>
        <div class="val">~0.5<span class="unit">s</span></div>
        <div class="desc">Our own staging proof: blind compute on an encrypted genetic vector, the server computes on ciphertext and never holds the key. Demonstrated, not theorized</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

